# @[or Int Null] annotation syntax: type-stage `or` keyword maps to Union(Int, Null).
# `or` is the type-stage function name for union — it maps directly to Type::Union
# without needing runtime eval machinery. `Null` is the empty record type.
# The value 42 satisfies Union(Int, Null) because Int is a member.
# TypeAssert form: [@[or Int Null] 42] checks 42 against Union(Int, Null).
[@[or Int Null] 42]
=== out
Int(42)
